<title>RUSSIA: Russia Jan trade surplus widens to $2.7 bln.</title>
<headline>Russia Jan trade surplus widens to $2.7 bln.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia posted a trade surplus of $2.7 billion in January this year after a $1.6 billion surplus in January 1996, the State Statistics Committee said.</p>
<p>Total trade, including other members of CIS</p>
<p>    RUSSIAN MERCHANDISE TRADE   Jan 97	Dec 96	Jan 96</p>
<p>    exports			     6.4	   7.5	   n/a</p>
<p>    imports			     3.7	   4.7	   n/a</p>
<p>    trade balance		    +2.7	  +2.8	  +1.6</p>
<p>Excluding trade with other members of CIS</p>
<p>    RUSSIAN MERCHANDISE TRADE   Jan 97	Dec 96	Jan 96</p>
<p>    exports			     5.1	   6.4	   n/a</p>
<p>    imports			     2.6	   3.5	   n/a</p>
<p>    trade balance		    +2.5	  +2.9	   n/a</p>
<p>Notes -- Figures in billion dollars, FOB. December data subject to revision.</p>
<p>--Jonathan Lynn, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
